                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/1209: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-10-13T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 13,
                                1925—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>63. Your telegrams Nos. 96, October 12, 11 a.m., and 97, October 12, 3 p.m. Your
                    action approved. Observe situation closely with a view to initiating measures
                    for retirement of United States troops as soon as, in your opinion and in that
                    of Canal Zone authorities, disorderly tendencies have abated sufficiently to
                    permit withdrawal. Continue to keep Department informed by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
